.TH CRUNCH_SYSFS_NAME 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_sysfs_name \- look up a filesystem type name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/legacy_syscalls.h>
.B int crunch_sysfs_name(int index, char *buffer);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses the obsolete Linux sysfs syscall to look up a filesystem type by index.
The output buffer must hold at least 256 bytes. Availability and permissions
depend on the kernel.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crunch_sysfs (3crunch),
.BR sysfs (2)
